msgid "As part of the BPMN authoring and review process, every innermost swimlane in a BPMN diagram SHALL correspond to an ActorDefinition resource. A lane names its ActorDefinition by id: its {code0} (a top-level {code1} whose {code2} is the ActorDefinition's FSH {code3} id), or else its own {code4}. A lane is never matched by its display name or by a file name. The <a0>{code5}</a0> tool in the smart-base knowledge graph checks this, together with the diagram's structure and the absence of Camunda or Zeebe extensions, on every pull request that changes a {code6}."
msgstr ""

